# Layout

## Width strategy

Content is **fluid at 100%** of the main region width, with **constant lateral
gutters only** (`--space-16` on the main padding). No centered max-width column.

- Operational surfaces (Overview, Match, Calendrier, Classements): fill the main
  area edge-to-gutter.
- Forms / focused tasks / dialogs: constrained width (28–40rem), never full width.
- Text never touches the viewport edge — gutters handle that, not a narrow column.

## Asymmetric composition ("asymétrie signifiante")

- The dominant region must visibly weigh more: hero band ≈ 1.6/1,
  two-column groups ≈ 1.45/1 (`dlab-grid-2--major`), never mechanical 50/50
  unless the two blocks are true peers.
- The reading order is: situation (top-left, largest) → next action (top-right)
  → pending work → detail.

## Density

- Standard density everywhere; grids may be denser but rows stay ≥ 40px tall.
- Whitespace between groups > whitespace inside groups.

## Responsive

Three **independent** breakpoint tiers — do not unify into a single value.

| Tier | Threshold | Role | SoT in Git |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Shell chrome** | phone `<48rem` · tablet `48–64rem` · desktop `≥64rem` | Rail overlay / icon-rail / expanded nav | `layout/viewportBreakpoints.ts`, `shell/useShellViewport.ts` |
| **Page grids** | `52rem` (`max-width: 51.999rem` narrow) | Two-column operational surfaces (Overview, Organisation, Matchs, Classements, Équipes split) | same + page CSS |
| **DS composition** | `56rem` | Asymmetric panel pairs collapse | `design-system/foundations/panels.css` |

Accueil (hors Shell): compact chrome at **48rem** (same as shell phone).

Équipes below **52rem**: master-detail — checkbox = bulk selection (list stays visible); tile body = open roster (detail full width). Header ops row: plateau left, selection bar + Add right (`teams__ops-row`). See Notion page **Équipes** § Responsive.

Legacy rule: two-column groups collapse below **56rem**, dominant block first.
